 "diagnosis": {
  "cause": "Vitest 4.1's pool (cli-api schedule/isEqualRunner) keeps a non-isolated worker only while the next queued file has the same project and environment; otherwise it terminates the worker and starts a new one. The single shared project held both node and jsdom files, which BaseSequencer orders by cached duration, so environments interleaved: 31 of the 46 shared jsdom files built a fresh jsdom window (~215 ms each, 7.0 s cumulative), and every switch also restarted a worker that re-imported its externalized dependencies.",
  "notWasteful": "src/testing/setup-dom.ts costs 0.5-0.7 s cumulative across 345 files (vi.resetModules plus jsdom global restore); collect (import) time is dominated by per-file re-evaluation of source modules after vi.resetModules, which the shared project's isolation contract requires; the isolated project (43 vi.mock files) builds one worker and environment per file by design (36 jsdom files, 7.4-7.6 s of environment setup)",
  "testHeavyFiles": "The slowest files are test work, not setup: scripts/qa/browser-lease.test.mjs 6.0 s, src/engine/core.test.ts 5.4 s, scripts/qa/run-scenario-slots.test.mjs 5.2 s, src/engine/fold/fold.test.ts 4.9 s, scripts/setup-assets.test.ts 3.1-3.4 s, scripts/friction-triggers.test.mjs 3.0 s. They are within budget and outside this bead's Areas; no file change is proposed."
 },
 "change": {
  "file": "vitest.config.ts",
  "what": "shared files whose source carries an @vitest-environment jsdom pragma (and no vi.mock) move to a separate non-isolated project, shared-dom, so each environment's files run contiguously and workers are reused. Workers stay at 2, isolation semantics, setup file, coverage and file set are unchanged (345 files, 4827 tests in every run).",
  "effect": "shared-dom jsdom environment builds 31 -> 2 (environment 7.0 s -> 0.6 s cumulative); shared node collect 19.4 s -> 16.3 s; suite environment phase 12.5-14.8 s -> 8.0-8.2 s; import 34.9-40.6 s -> 28.4-32.5 s"
 },
 "beforeMedianS": 56.525,
 "afterMedianS": 46.84,
 "conclusion": "The full suite meets D19's 60 s at low host load before the change (median 56.5 s at load 4.4-6.8, 6 runs) with 1-4 s of headroom. Grouping the shared files by environment cuts it to a median 46.8 s (45.9-49.5 s, 3 interleaved runs at load 3.5-7.5), about -9.7 s (-17%). Budget unchanged.",
